From dada87c0fce3e5975e6d1506466a71927fe439d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikita Nedoshovenko <nikita.nedoshovenko@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:51:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add Ukrainian/Russian language layer, move demo to Vincennes

- Gemini prompts handle UA/RU/EN radio procedure, callsigns, corrections, number words, drone slang
- Per-callsign unit memory; UA and RU spellings of a callsign are one unit
- Landmark resolution: unit positions, mission codenames, alias table, then Nominatim
- Shape-aware placement with uncertainty circles (offsets from edges, not centres)
- Drone/enemy sightings become fused threat markers across units
- New /api/process-text and /api/markers endpoints, text input fallback in the UI
- Map shows each unit, uncertainty circles and threat markers
- Stop tracking backend/.env (the committed key must be revoked)
- Offline end-to-end test with fake Gemini and geocoder

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KG2RA2i89hGvASt44B7U7K
